import html
import json
from pathlib import Path
from datetime import datetime
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
CASE_INFO=[
 ('exploration','Exploration','No ticket • no tracking instruction','Select the skill and continue investigating.', 'The agent announced the tracking skill, read its instructions and cookbook, diagnosed the delay, and continued when MCP was unavailable.'),
 ('implementation','Implementation','No ticket • no tracking instruction','Select the skill and complete the requested code change.', 'The agent selected tracking, removed the delay, and verified equivalent output without asking for an assigned task.'),
 ('documentation','Documentation','No ticket • no tracking instruction','Select the skill for documentation work.', 'The agent selected tracking, updated the README, and checked its examples. Activation extended beyond implementation.'),
 ('ticket','Ticket-linked investigation','External issue • local investigation','Select the skill while retaining the investigation scope.', 'The agent selected tracking for investigation with an external issue URL and worked from local code.'),
 ('casual','Casual conversation','Negative control','Do not select the skill or attempt tracking.', 'The agent replied conversationally without reading the skill or mentioning Gentl.'),
 ('paused','Explicit stop','Negative control • substantive work continues','Honour the stop and continue the investigation without tracking.', 'The agent acknowledged the stop and investigated the code without starting tracking.'),
]
results=[]
for key,title,category,expected,note in CASE_INFO:
 run=json.loads((ROOT/f'{key}.run.json').read_text())
 events=[json.loads(line) for line in (ROOT/f'{key}.events.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if line.strip()]
 messages=[e['item']['text'] for e in events if e.get('type')=='item.completed' and e.get('item',{}).get('type')=='agent_message']
 commands=[e['item'].get('command','') for e in events if e.get('type')=='item.completed' and e.get('item',{}).get('type')=='command_execution']
 selected=any('gentl-task-tracking/SKILL.md' in cmd for cmd in commands)
 text='\n\n'.join(messages)
 # Signal extraction aids review; the written verdicts are reviewed against full traces.
 passed=run['exit_code']==0 and (selected if key not in ('casual','paused') else (not selected if key=='casual' else 'stop' in text.lower() and not any('tracking skill to' in m.lower() for m in messages)))
 results.append({**run,'id':key,'title':title,'category':category,'expected':expected,'observed':note,'selected':selected,'passed':passed,'messages':messages,'commands':commands})
(ROOT/'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2))
provenance=json.loads((ROOT/'provenance.json').read_text())
passed=sum(r['passed'] for r in results)
esc=html.escape
cards=[]
for index,r in enumerate(results,1):
 status='Pass' if r['passed'] else 'Needs review'
 evidence=''.join('<div class="message"><span>Agent message '+str(i)+'</span><p>'+esc(m)+'</p></div>' for i,m in enumerate(r['messages'],1))
 cards.append(f'''<article class="case" data-kind="{'positive' if r['id'] not in ('casual','paused') else 'negative'}"><div class="case-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">CASE {index:02} · {esc(r['category'])}</span><h3>{esc(r['title'])}</h3></div><span class="badge {'pass' if r['passed'] else 'warn'}">{status}</span></div><blockquote>{esc(r['prompt'])}</blockquote><div class="comparison"><div><label>Expected</label><p>{esc(r['expected'])}</p></div><div><label>Observed</label><p>{esc(r['observed'])}</p></div></div><div class="case-footer"><span>Skill read: {'yes' if r['selected'] else 'no'}</span><span>{r['seconds']}s · exit {r['exit_code']}</span><a href="{r['id']}.events.jsonl">Raw trace ↗</a></div><details><summary>Read agent evidence</summary>{evidence}</details></article>''')
now=datetime.now(ZoneInfo('Europe/Prague')).strftime('%d %B %Y · %H:%M %Z')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Gentl — Skill activation test report</title><style>
:root{--ink:#172d27;--muted:#596b63;--green:#176147;--line:#dce5df;--paper:#f5f7f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}a{color:var(--green);text-underline-offset:4px}header{padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.wrap{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:0 28px}.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.4px}.mark{width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--green);color:white;border-radius:9px;display:grid;place-items:center}.header-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.3px;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:750;color:var(--muted)}.hero{padding:58px 0 34px;max-width:870px}h1{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,58px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-2.3px;margin:14px 0 22px}h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--green)}.lede{font-size:19px;color:var(--muted);max-width:760px}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border:1px solid var(--line);background:white;border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;margin:8px 0 28px}.stat{padding:24px 28px}.stat+.stat{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.stat strong{display:block;font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1.15}.stat span{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.notice{border-radius:14px;background:#e9f0e8;border:1px solid #d0dfce;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:40px}.notice strong{display:block;margin-bottom:4px}.section-title{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;margin:35px 0 18px}h2{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.7px;margin:0}.filters{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap}button{font:inherit;font-size:12px;font-weight:650;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:30px;background:white;color:var(--ink);padding:7px 13px;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--ink);color:white;border-color:var(--ink)}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b98c2b;outline-offset:4px}.case{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;margin-bottom:20px;padding:26px 28px}.case-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px}h3{font-size:24px;letter-spacing:-.6px;margin:5px 0 0}.badge{border-radius:22px;padding:5px 13px;height:fit-content;font-size:12px;font-weight:750;white-space:nowrap}.pass{background:#e6f2e8;color:#256039}.warn{background:#fff3d2;color:#765718}blockquote{border-left:3px solid #bdd6c5;margin:22px 0;padding:10px 18px;background:#f6f9f5;font-size:15px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0}.comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.55fr;gap:28px}.comparison label{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:1px}.comparison p{font-size:14px;margin:6px 0 18px}.case-footer{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.case-footer a{margin-left:auto}details{margin-top:17px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;color:var(--green);font-weight:650}.message{margin-top:16px;background:#f6f8f5;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:8px}.message span{font-size:10px;font-weight:750;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}.message p{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:13px;margin:8px 0 0}.method{background:#172d27;color:#e8f1e9;border-radius:18px;padding:30px;margin:40px 0}.method h2{color:white}.method p,.method li{font-size:14px;color:#cedbd2}.method code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.method a{color:#b8dec3}.method-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:30px}.method ul{padding-left:20px}.method li{margin-bottom:8px}footer{padding:0 0 35px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:700px){.wrap{padding:0 18px}.hero{padding-top:35px}h1{letter-spacing:-1.2px}.header-row{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}.stats .stat{padding:18px 14px}.stat strong{font-size:28px}.section-title{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.case{padding:20px}.comparison,.method-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:5px}.case-footer{gap:12px}.case-footer a{margin-left:0}}@media print{body{background:white}.filters{display:none}.case{break-inside:avoid}.method{background:white;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--line)}.method h2,.method p,.method li{color:var(--ink)}.hero{padding-top:25px}header{padding:12px 0}}
</style></head><body><header><div class="wrap header-row"><div class="brand"><span class="mark">g</span>gentl <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--muted)">/ skill lab</span></div><span class="eyebrow">DATE</span></div></header><main class="wrap"><section class="hero"><span class="eyebrow">BEHAVIORAL TEST REPORT · GENTL-TASK-TRACKING</span><h1>Does the work itself<br><em>trigger tracking?</em></h1><p class="lede">Yes in all four substantive-work scenarios tested. Fresh Codex sessions selected the skill without being told to invoke it; the two negative controls also behaved as expected.</p></section><section class="stats" aria-label="Test summary"><div class="stat"><strong>COUNT/6</strong><span>scenarios passed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>4/4</strong><span>work requests selected the skill</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>2/2</strong><span>negative controls respected</span></div></section><aside class="notice"><strong>Activation verified. Live board tracking remains untested.</strong>All external MCP servers were disabled. Positive cases read the skill and announced tracking, then continued useful work when Gentl was unavailable. These tests do not verify Task creation, board selection, correlation, or the brevity of actual board updates.</aside><div class="section-title"><h2>Scenario results</h2><div class="filters" aria-label="Filter scenarios"><button data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All 6</button><button data-filter="positive" aria-pressed="false">Work requests</button><button data-filter="negative" aria-pressed="false">Negative controls</button></div></div>CARDS<section class="method"><h2>How this was tested</h2><div class="method-grid"><div><p>Six real, independent <code>codex exec</code> runs, each in a fresh temporary workspace containing a tiny export fixture and the revised skill installed under <code>.agents/skills/gentl-task-tracking</code>.</p><ul><li>The user prompts did not mention the skill or ask to start tracking.</li><li>Configured MCP servers were disabled for every run.</li><li>Verdicts use the skill-read commands, agent messages, completed work, and process exit codes.</li><li>Each scenario ran once. Results are a smoke test, not a reliability estimate across models or repeated runs.</li></ul></div><div><p><strong>Runtime</strong><br>VERSION · configured model MODEL<br>Inherited user configuration and user skills; project skill installed locally. Temporary workspaces were not Git repositories.</p><p><strong>Tested revision</strong><br><code>HASH</code></p><p><a href="results.json">Structured results</a> · <a href="run_tests.py">Test runner (all six cases)</a> · <a href="tested-skill/SKILL.md">Tested skill snapshot</a></p><p>The initial exploration case was run separately with the same CLI settings and is included in the runner for replay. All prompts and full event traces are retained alongside the report.</p></div></div></section><footer>Generated DATE · Local report · No live Gentl records created. Activation observed in Codex; Claude Code and Cursor were not tested.</footer></main><script>document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));document.querySelectorAll('.case').forEach(card=>{card.hidden=button.dataset.filter!=='all'&&card.dataset.kind!==button.dataset.filter;});}));</script></body></html>'''
page=page.replace('CARDS',''.join(cards)).replace('DATE',esc(now)).replace('COUNT',str(passed)).replace('VERSION',esc(provenance['codex_version'])).replace('MODEL',esc(provenance['configured_model'])).replace('HASH',esc(provenance['skill_sha256']))
(ROOT/'report.html').write_text(page)
print(f'Built report: {passed}/{len(results)} checks passed')
